+# Daily Grind components
+
+Load `daily-grind.js` once using a module script. It registers three independent
+custom elements with open shadow roots and no dependencies or build step.
+
+```html
+<script type="module" src="./components/daily-grind.js"></script>
+
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">Cold Brew</h3>
+  <p>Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/cold-brew"
+     aria-label="View details for Cold Brew">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+| Element | Named slots | Default slot | Exposed part |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `coffee-card` | `heading`, `action` | Description | `card` |
+| `grind-hero` | `heading`, `action` | Supporting content | `hero` |
+| `grind-navigation` | `brand` | Navigation anchors | `navigation` |
+
+Place slot content directly inside the component. Use native heading elements at
+the appropriate level and native anchors for navigation. Give repeated action
+links distinct accessible names. Slotted content stays in the document, so links
+and headings remain available without JavaScript, and edits update automatically.
+Component styles target top-level slotted elements; consumers own nested content.
+
+The navigation's mobile disclosure uses a native button, `aria-expanded`, and a
+same-shadow-root `aria-controls` target. Below 48rem it starts collapsed; Enter
+or Space toggles it, and Escape closes it and returns focus to the button. Link
+activation also closes it. Desktop links are always visible, and resizing moves
+focus away from controls that become hidden. Each instance owns its listeners,
+removing them when disconnected and restoring them when reconnected.
+
+Theme through inherited `--primary`, `--text`, and `--accent` properties. Cards
+also accept `--coffee-card-background`; the hero accepts `--grind-hero-image`
+(a CSS `url(...)` value). All have standalone defaults. Use `::part(card)`,
+`::part(hero)`, or `::part(navigation)` for additional container styling. Hosts
+are not extra tab stops; keyboard navigation uses the native links and button.
+
+Global `styles.css` owns page layout, footer styles, skip navigation, and basic
+unupgraded-element fallbacks. Component styling stays inside shadow templates.
diff --git a/components/daily-grind.js b/components/daily-grind.js
